WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.459
Metro and Bus.

2
00:00:01.739 --> 00:00:06.070
Day 26 of the Soft Skill Playbook course, in the Everyday Life phase.

3
00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:08.844
The key idea.

4
00:00:09.124 --> 00:00:18.383
Today's goal: buy tickets or cards, find the right route, ask where to get off, and handle crowded or confusing rides on the metro and city buses.

5
00:00:19.733 --> 00:00:20.586
Part 1.

6
00:00:20.866 --> 00:00:21.826
Key words.

7
00:00:23.076 --> 00:00:24.441
Here is a quick table:

8
00:00:24.721 --> 00:00:38.865
Word or phrase, and Meaning. smart card or travel card: a card you top up and tap at the gate. top up or recharge: add money to the card. token or single-journey ticket: one-time ticket. line (Purple Line,

9
00:00:39.145 --> 00:00:58.132
Line 2): a metro route. interchange or change at...: station where you switch lines. towards or direction: which way the train is going (towards Whitefield). platform or gate or exit: where you board or enter or leave. bus stop or bus stand or depot: where buses stop or start.

10
00:00:59.482 --> 00:01:13.434
route number: the bus number (for example, 500D). conductor: person who sells tickets on the bus. pass (daily or monthly): unlimited travel for a period. rush hour or peak hours: busiest times.

11
00:01:14.784 --> 00:01:15.659
Part 2.

12
00:01:15.939 --> 00:01:17.155
Questions you'll ask.

13
00:01:18.405 --> 00:01:19.194
Metro.

14
00:01:19.474 --> 00:01:21.543
How much is a ticket to MG Road?

15
00:01:21.823 --> 00:01:23.445
Can I top up my card here?

16
00:01:23.725 --> 00:01:25.431
Which line goes to the airport?

17
00:01:25.711 --> 00:01:27.247
Do I need to change trains?

18
00:01:27.527 --> 00:01:28.658
Where do I change?

19
00:01:28.938 --> 00:01:31.327
Which platform for trains towards Whitefield?

20
00:01:31.607 --> 00:01:33.655
How many stops is it to Indiranagar?

21
00:01:33.935 --> 00:01:36.090
Which exit is closest to the bus stand?

22
00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:39.275
What time is the last train tonight?

23
00:01:40.625 --> 00:01:41.350
Bus.

24
00:01:41.630 --> 00:01:43.827
Does this bus go to the railway station?

25
00:01:44.107 --> 00:01:46.283
Which bus should I take for Koramangala?

26
00:01:46.563 --> 00:01:48.718
How often does the 500D come?

27
00:01:48.998 --> 00:01:50.939
How much is the fare to Silk Board?

28
00:01:51.219 --> 00:01:53.822
Could you tell me when we get to the hospital stop?

29
00:01:54.102 --> 00:01:56.321
Is this the right stop for the airport bus?

30
00:01:56.601 --> 00:01:58.286
Where should I get off for the market?

31
00:01:59.636 --> 00:02:00.532
Part 3.

32
00:02:00.812 --> 00:02:02.177
Questions you'll be asked.

33
00:02:03.427 --> 00:02:04.793
Here is a quick table:

34
00:02:05.073 --> 00:02:06.609
They ask, and You answer.

35
00:02:06.889 --> 00:02:07.785
Where to?:

36
00:02:08.065 --> 00:02:09.409
MG Road, please.

37
00:02:09.689 --> 00:02:10.627
One ticket.

38
00:02:10.907 --> 00:02:12.230
Single or return?:

39
00:02:12.510 --> 00:02:13.577
Single, please.

40
00:02:13.857 --> 00:02:15.073
Do you have a card?:

41
00:02:15.353 --> 00:02:18.211
Yes, I'd like to top it up with 500 rupees.

42
00:02:18.491 --> 00:02:19.686
Do you have change?:

43
00:02:19.966 --> 00:02:22.739
Sorry, I only have a 500 rupeesnote.

44
00:02:23.019 --> 00:02:24.534
Can I pay by UPI?

45
00:02:24.814 --> 00:02:25.603
Ticket?

46
00:02:25.883 --> 00:02:26.801
(conductor):

47
00:02:27.081 --> 00:02:30.110
Here's my pass. / One to Majestic, please.

48
00:02:31.460 --> 00:02:32.377
Part 4.

49
00:02:32.657 --> 00:02:35.495
Conversation 1: at the metro ticket counter.

50
00:02:36.745 --> 00:02:38.771
Here is how the conversation goes.

51
00:02:39.051 --> 00:02:39.777
Hi.

52
00:02:40.057 --> 00:02:42.638
I'd like a ticket to Cubbon Park, please.

53
00:02:42.918 --> 00:02:44.113
Single journey?

54
00:02:44.393 --> 00:02:45.097
Yes.

55
00:02:45.377 --> 00:02:48.001
Actually, I'll be travelling every day.

56
00:02:48.281 --> 00:02:50.435
Can I get a smart card instead?

57
00:02:50.715 --> 00:02:51.419
Sure.

58
00:02:51.699 --> 00:02:54.686
The card is 50, rupeesand you can add any amount.

59
00:02:54.966 --> 00:02:55.713
Great.

60
00:02:55.993 --> 00:02:59.854
Please add 500. rupeesCan I pay by UPI?

61
00:03:01.204 --> 00:03:02.804
The conversation continues.

62
00:03:03.084 --> 00:03:04.279
Yes, scan here.

63
00:03:04.559 --> 00:03:05.241
Done.

64
00:03:05.521 --> 00:03:08.380
Which platform should I go to for Cubbon Park?

65
00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:10.687
Platform 1, towards Challaghatta.

66
00:03:10.967 --> 00:03:12.247
It's four stops.

67
00:03:12.527 --> 00:03:14.425
Do I need to change trains?

68
00:03:14.705 --> 00:03:16.028
No, it's direct.

69
00:03:17.378 --> 00:03:18.978
The conversation continues.

70
00:03:19.258 --> 00:03:20.175
Thank you!

71
00:03:21.525 --> 00:03:22.485
Part 5.

72
00:03:22.765 --> 00:03:25.923
Conversation 2: on the bus, not sure where to get off.

73
00:03:27.173 --> 00:03:29.199
Here is how the conversation goes.

74
00:03:29.479 --> 00:03:32.231
Excuse me, does this bus go to St.

75
00:03:32.511 --> 00:03:33.877
John's Hospital?

76
00:03:34.157 --> 00:03:35.010
Yes.

77
00:03:35.290 --> 00:03:36.207
Ticket?

78
00:03:36.487 --> 00:03:37.597
One to St.

79
00:03:37.877 --> 00:03:39.114
John's, please.

80
00:03:39.394 --> 00:03:40.738
How much is it?

81
00:03:41.018 --> 00:03:42.469
25 rupees.

82
00:03:42.749 --> 00:03:43.815
Here you go.

83
00:03:44.095 --> 00:03:45.973
Could you tell me when we get there?

84
00:03:46.253 --> 00:03:47.981
I'm not from this area.

85
00:03:49.331 --> 00:03:50.931
The conversation continues.

86
00:03:51.211 --> 00:03:53.131
Okay, it's about fifteen minutes.

87
00:03:53.411 --> 00:03:54.648
Twenty minutes later

88
00:03:54.928 --> 00:03:58.021
Excuse me, have we passed the hospital stop?

89
00:03:58.301 --> 00:04:00.392
No, it's the next one, after the signal.

90
00:04:00.672 --> 00:04:02.080
Thank you so much!

91
00:04:03.430 --> 00:04:05.030
The conversation continues.

92
00:04:05.310 --> 00:04:06.654
Hospital stop!

93
00:04:06.934 --> 00:04:08.065
Get down here.

94
00:04:08.345 --> 00:04:09.155
Thanks!

95
00:04:10.505 --> 00:04:11.444
Part 6.

96
00:04:11.724 --> 00:04:12.897
When things go wrong.

97
00:04:14.147 --> 00:04:15.619
The gate isn't opening.

98
00:04:15.899 --> 00:04:17.222
My card has balance.

99
00:04:17.502 --> 00:04:18.569
Could you check it?

100
00:04:18.849 --> 00:04:20.790
I tapped in but forgot to tap out.

101
00:04:21.070 --> 00:04:22.137
What should I do?

102
00:04:22.417 --> 00:04:23.910
I took the wrong direction.

103
00:04:24.190 --> 00:04:25.982
How do I go back to Majestic?

104
00:04:26.262 --> 00:04:29.889
Sorry, is anyone sitting here? / Could you move in a little, please?

105
00:04:30.169 --> 00:04:32.707
Excuse me, I need to get off at the next stop.

106
00:04:34.057 --> 00:04:34.996
Part 7.

107
00:04:35.276 --> 00:04:36.193
Practice.

108
00:04:37.443 --> 00:04:47.043
Make questions for these answers: ? then No, you need to change at Majestic. ? then Every ten minutes. ? then Take exit B, it's right next to the bus stand.

109
00:04:48.393 --> 00:04:49.311
Success:

110
00:04:49.591 --> 00:04:50.444
Answers.

111
00:04:50.724 --> 00:04:54.756
Is this train direct to the airport? / Do I need to change trains?

112
00:04:55.036 --> 00:04:57.063
How often does the bus or train come?

113
00:04:57.343 --> 00:04:58.089
3.

114
00:04:58.369 --> 00:05:00.524
Which exit is closest to the bus stand?

115
00:05:01.874 --> 00:05:02.749
Part 8.

116
00:05:03.029 --> 00:05:04.074
Speak today.

117
00:05:05.324 --> 00:05:09.143
Ask one Does this bus go to...? or Which platform...? question.

118
00:05:09.423 --> 00:05:12.559
Read the metro or bus map and say your route out loud:

119
00:05:12.839 --> 00:05:15.207
I take Line 1 towards... change at...

120
00:05:16.557 --> 00:05:18.093
That's the end of this lesson.

121
00:05:18.373 --> 00:05:23.045
Pick one script from it, say it out loud three times, and use it for real today.

122
00:05:23.325 --> 00:05:29.426
For extra practice, paste the Master Prompt into an AI assistant and role-play the conversation.

